they work like detectives trying to  trace a silent  killer ebola health workers questioned  the son of a nurse who died from the  virus in early february  asking questions on what she ate where  she went  and what she did did he see anything  unusual  before her death still in shock he calls  out to his deceased mother  mom i can't stop crying people say you  died of ebola  but we don't really know is this true  are they lying to us  god only knows i feel powerless night  and day i cry  why did you have to go he is not alone  in doubting ebola's resurgence  at the epicenter of the outbreak the  regional market is bustling despite a  ban on public gatherings  worse meat from wild animals known to  harbor ebola  is sold in stalls  what you are seeing here is not a big  deal people are just informed some  haven't come to the market  but those people you see here are  foreigners from neighboring countries  in 2015 more than 11 000 people died and  20 000  were infected after the virus spread  from guinea's forest region  to neighboring liberia and sierra leone  the outbreak was contained  after an experimental vaccine was  distributed but not before health  workers were attacked by people who did  not believe in the virus  infected patients were kept in isolation  and the dead were taken away  buried without their families being  present  a good lesson we learned is that instead  of doing everything by ourselves we  have to give the resources and the means  to the population and to the localized  workers  the local authorities to manage that  break by themselves  we cannot continue coming with big wild  suv and with a lot of people in small  villages  eleven thousand vaccines and two hundred  health workers have just arrived in  guinea's capital konakui to help manage  this latest outbreak the doses will go  to front-line health workers  and close contacts patients are being  treated in  nzerikore konakri and little by the  malian border  almost a month after lua's mother died  of ebola  the virus is spreading nicholas hawk al  jazeera
 

